[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_mnd1t")
name = "Deuteranopia (CVD)"
icon = ExtResource("1_05ify")
short_info = "SEMANTIC MEANING BOUND TO HUE CHANNEL ONLY"
manual_text = "[b][u]CLINICAL OVERVIEW[/u][/b]
Color Vision Deficiency (CVD) is a visual condition in which people have difficulty distinguishing specific colors or color shades. It is caused by abnormalities in the cone cells of the retina that detect color.

[b][u]VARIATIONS & DEMOGRAPHICS[/u][/b]
[indent]
[b]•[/b] The most common form is red-green deficiency (also called Deuteranopia), although blue-yellow deficiency and complete color blindness are rarer forms.
[b]•[/b] It affects men more frequently because the related genes are linked to the X chromosome.
[b]•[/b] Diagnosis is commonly performed through color vision tests like the Ishihara test.
[b]•[/b] There is currently no cure for inherited CVD, though assistive technologies may help in some situations.
[/indent]"
related_wcag = ExtResource("1_2x1d4")
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://dry85ilgnq64e"
